      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a section you can add to directly address the traditionalist concerns.\n\nSome may view this as political \"feel-good\" initiative, but this perspective fundamentally misinterprets the modern definition of robust fiduciary duty. In the current market, true long-term value *is* intrinsically tied to strong governance and responsible environmental and social performance because these factors mitigate hidden systemic and operational risks for the firm.\n\nTherefore, aggressive capital allocation towards impact is not a deviation from our duty to maximize value, but rather a sophisticated, necessary evolution of it, ensuring the company is built to generate superior, stable, and enduring shareholder returns for the next decades, not just the next quarter.",
      "source": "target",
